The headline survives the easy wrong reading: “agreed to decide” does not announce a detention ruling or endorse a population count. The first sentence says what happened, and no person is named before introduction. The dek gives the old practice and new position. The first paragraph then leans on “applicant for admission” and “seeking admission” before explaining their difference, and spends 75 words on the statutory clause and exceptions. **The top fails a cold reader there**, despite an accurate headline and first sentence.

